 "id": "2026-11-19-gaza-tanks-yellow-line",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Israeli tanks just crossed Gaza's ceasefire line. Is the truce over?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "For the first time since the October 2025 ceasefire, Israeli tanks pushed past the so-called Yellow Line in central Gaza. The army and Shin Bet say the target is a tunnel near the Nuseirat and Bureij camps. Families were ordered to leave their homes."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Hamas calls it a flagrant violation. Witnesses say tanks reached Salah al-Din Road, Gaza's main north-south highway. Gaza health authorities say more than sixteen hundred Palestinians have been killed since the ceasefire began. Israel says five of its soldiers died."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Formally, the truce still stands. But a Board of Peace report to the UN Security Council faults both sides: Israel for restricting aid, Hamas for armed activity. Israel's defence minister says troops stay until Hamas is dismantled."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Gaza ceasefire hold into the new year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
