 "upload": {
  "title": "Israeli Tanks Push Past Gaza's Yellow Line #shorts",
  "description": "Israeli tanks advanced west of the so-called Yellow Line in central Gaza on November 18, 2026, in the first such ground push beyond the ceasefire boundary since the truce took effect on October 10, 2025, according to Reuters and AFP. The Israeli military and the Shin Bet security service said the operation targeted a tunnel and Hamas infrastructure near the Nuseirat and Bureij refugee camps, and residents were ordered to leave homes in the area. Witnesses said some tanks reached Salah al-Din Road, Gaza's main north-south highway. Hamas called the operation a flagrant violation of the ceasefire. Gaza health authorities say more than 1,600 Palestinians have been killed since the ceasefire began; the Israeli military says five of its soldiers have been killed in that period. A Board of Peace report to the UN Security Council, seen by Reuters, faulted both sides: it accused Israel of restricting aid and Hamas of continuing armed activity. Israel's Defence Minister Israel Katz has said troops will stay until Hamas is dismantled. The course of the Yellow Line on the map is approximate. Casualty figures could not be independently verified.\n\nSources:\nReuters via NBC News / IBTimes, Nov 18, 2026: Israeli tanks roll into central Gaza in first ground operation since ceasefire began\nAFP via France 24, Nov 18, 2026: Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line\nAl Jazeera, Nov 18, 2026: What does Israel's new ground offensive mean for Palestinians in Gaza?\nTimes of Israel, Nov 18, 2026: IDF launches rare Gaza operation beyond Yellow Line, orders civilians out\nXinhua, Nov 19, 2026: Israel announces ground operation beyond Gaza ceasefire line\n\n#geopolitics #Gaza #Israel #ceasefire",
